# Agent lifecycle state

The agent subcommand should publish each supported lifecycle state to the
invoking tmux pane's `@smth.agent.state` user option.

    :bins env

> [!NOTE]
> 'env' is available.

    :$ smth agent idle (exit: 0)
    :t show-options -pqv @smth.agent.state (success)

```
idle
```

    :$ smth agent running (exit: 0)
    :t show-options -pqv @smth.agent.state (success)

```
running
```

    :$ smth agent waiting (exit: 0)
    :t show-options -pqv @smth.agent.state (success)

```
waiting
```

    :$ smth agent succeeded --title "release ready" --summary "ready now" (exit: 0)
    :t show-options -pqv @smth.agent.state (success)

```
succeeded
```

    :$ smth agent failed --title -still-titled --summary -still-safe (exit: 0)
    :t show-options -pqv @smth.agent.state (success)

```
failed
```

The command should target `$TMUX_PANE`, even when it identifies a pane other
than tmux's active pane.

    :t split-window -d -t 0:0 (success)
    :$ env TMUX_PANE=0:0.1 smth agent waiting (exit: 0)
    :t show-options -pqv -t 0:0.1 @smth.agent.state (success)

```
waiting
```

    :t show-options -pqv -t 0:0.0 @smth.agent.state (success)

```
failed
```

Exiting agent tracking should remove the pane option.

    :$ smth agent exit (exit: 0)
    :t show-options -pqv @smth.agent.state (success)

Unsupported actions should be rejected before tmux metadata is changed.

    :$ smth agent running (exit: 0)
    :$ smth agent start (exit: 2)

```stderr
error: invalid value 'start' for '<ACTION>'
  [possible values: idle, running, waiting, succeeded, failed, exit]

For more information, try '--help'.
```

    :t show-options -pqv @smth.agent.state (success)

```
running
```

    :$ smth agent exit (exit: 0)
    :t show-options -pqv @smth.agent.state (success)

